● I have implemented the requirements for the Movie Rating API. Here is a
  summary of the changes:

  1. Rating Model (server/src/models/Rating.js)

  - Defined the schema with movieCode (required), rating (required, 1-5), note
    (optional), and ratedBy (optional, ref to User).
  - Enabled { timestamps: true }.
  - Added a compound unique index on { movieCode: 1, ratedBy: 1 } to ensure a
    user can only rate a movie once.

  2. Rating Controller (server/src/controllers/ratingController.js)

  - Validation: Implemented a Joi schema for createRating to validate inputs.
  - createRating: Validates the request body, creates the rating, and returns
    201. It also handles MongoDB duplicate key errors (code 11000) by returning
    a 409 Conflict status.
  - getAllRatings: Fetches all ratings using .lean() for better performance.
  - getRating: Fetches a specific rating by ID, returning 404 if not found.
  - getRatingSummary:
    - Checks for the movieCode query parameter (returns 400 if missing).
    - Uses a MongoDB aggregation pipeline ($match $\rightarrow$ $group) to
      calculate the averageRating and ratingCount.
    - Handles cases with no ratings by returning 0 for both metrics.

  3. Rating Routes (server/src/routes/ratings.js)

  - Wired the controller functions to the API paths.
  - Critical Routing: Placed the /summary route before the /:id route to prevent
    Express from treating the string "summary" as a rating ID.

  The implementation follows the structural patterns established in the provided
  userController and User model.

